IMPORTANT NOTICE: BIOMEDICAL & HARDWARE SAFETY DISCLAIMER

1. NON-MEDICAL DEVICE NOTICE (ACADEMIC & PROTOTYPING USE ONLY):
   This system, including its source code, hardware schematics, firmware, signal
   processing algorithms, cloud infrastructure, and documentation, is developed
   solely for engineering education, academic research, and experimental prototyping.
   It is NOT a certified medical device under US FDA (21 CFR Part 870), European
   Union MDR (2017/745), ISO 13485, or the Vietnam Ministry of Health regulations.
   It must NEVER be used for clinical diagnosis, patient treatment, medical triage,
   critical care, or life-support applications. It cannot substitute for professional
   medical judgment, hospital-grade diagnostic monitors, or certified personal
   emergency response systems (PERS).

2. ELECTRICAL SAFETY & PATIENT ISOLATION WARNING (IEC 60601-1):
   The AD8232 ECG sensor module attaches conductive Ag/AgCl electrodes directly to
   human skin. To prevent lethal electrical shock and ventricular fibrillation from
   AC mains leakage currents, the wearable sensor node must ONLY be powered by
   isolated DC battery sources (such as Li-Po / Li-Ion cells or ungrounded battery packs).
   NEVER power or program the wearable sensor node using a USB charger connected to
   AC mains (110V/220V) or a computer plugged into AC mains without medical-grade
   galvanic isolation complying with IEC 60601-1 (Type BF/CF patient isolation).

3. ALGORITHMIC & TELECOMMUNICATION LIMITATIONS:
   Fall detection algorithms (acceleration magnitude and posture verification) and
   ECG peak detection algorithms (Pan-Tompkins) are subject to false positives
   (false alarms) and false negatives (missed falls or undetected arrhythmias).
   Telecommunication channels (Wi-Fi, UDP, MQTT, Telegram, Zalo) depend on
   third-party networks, internet connectivity, and external APIs. Delivery of alerts
   is strictly best-effort and cannot be guaranteed against network latency, packet
   loss, or cloud downtime.

4. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY:
   Under no circumstances shall the authors, copyright holders, or contributors
   be held liable for any direct, indirect, incidental, special, exemplary, or
   consequential damages, including but not limited to bodily injury, electrical
   shock, illness, misdiagnosis, loss of life, or property damage arising in any
   way out of the use, replication, modification, or deployment of this hardware
   and software.

